  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0174 database is designed to manage the operations and information of a hospital. It consists of 15 tables that store data about physicians, departments, medical procedures, patients, nurses, appointments, medications, and hospital rooms. The physician table contains information about each doctor, including their employee ID, name, position, and social security number. The department table stores details about each department, such as its ID, name, and head. The affiliated_with table links physicians to the departments they are affiliated with, while the trained_in table records the medical procedures each physician is certified in. The patient table holds information about each patient, including their social security number, name, address, phone number, insurance ID, and primary care physician ID. The nurse table stores details about each nurse, including their employee ID, name, position, registration status, and social security number. The appointments table schedules appointments for patients, including the patient's ID, nurse's ID, physician's ID, start and end times, and examination room. The medication table lists available medications, including their code, name, brand, and description. The prescribes table records the medications prescribed to patients, including the physician's ID, patient's ID, medication ID, date, appointment ID, and dose. The block table represents the hospital's layout, with each block consisting of a floor ID and a block code ID. The room table stores information about each room, including its number, type, block floor ID, block code ID, and availability status. The on_call table tracks which nurse is on call for each block and floor. The stay table records the duration of each patient's stay in the hospital, including their ID, patient ID, room ID, start and end times. The undergoes table tracks the medical procedures each patient undergoes, including their ID, patient ID, procedure ID, stay ID, date, physician ID, and assisting nurse ID.",
  "gold_question": "Healthcare Management System\n\n1) Background / Context:  \n   The project involves the development of a healthcare management system designed to streamline patient care and administrative processes in a healthcare facility. This system utilizes a relational database to manage comprehensive data about physicians, departments, medical procedures, patients, nurses, appointments, medications, rooms, and facility blocks.\n\n2) Objectives:  \n   - To enhance the efficiency of administrative tasks such as scheduling appointments, room assignments, and medication management.\n   - To improve patient care by providing quick access to accurate patient data and personalized treatment plans.\n   - To ensure regulatory compliance through accurate record-keeping and documentation.\n   - To optimize resource allocation and operational efficiency through automation and data-driven decisions.\n\n3) Stakeholders & Users:  \n   - Healthcare Administrators: Manage facility operations, crucial in oversight and compliance.\n   - Physicians & Nurses: Primary users for patient interaction, treatment documentation, and procedure management.\n   - Patients: Service beneficiaries who interact with the system for appointments and feedback.\n\n4) Functional Descriptions:  \n   - Physician Management: Store and manage physician details including employee ID, name, position, and SSN.\n   - Department Management: Oversee departments with information such as department ID, name, head, and affiliations with physicians.\n   - Medical Procedure Tracking: Maintain a database of medical procedure codes, names, and costs.\n   - Patient Management: Handle patient details including SSN, contact information, insurance, and selected primary care physician.\n   - Nurse Management: Record nurse information with details on registration and department assignments.\n   - Appointment Scheduling: Store and manage appointment data, including related patients, nurses, and physicians, with time and location specifics.\n   - Medication Management: Catalog medications by code, name, brand, and description.\n   - Room and Block Management: Manage room allocations and block details for patient stays and resource planning.\n   - History Tracking: Maintain records of patient procedures, stays, and prescribed medications.\n\n5) Non-Functional Descriptions:  \n   - Scalability: Support a growing database of patient and staff information.\n   - Security: Ensure data protection and privacy standards are strictly upheld, particularly for sensitive patient information.\n   - Usability: Provide an intuitive interface for healthcare professionals for quick data retrieval and entry.\n   - Reliability: Ensure system uptime for 24/7 healthcare operations and accurate data management.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_llama31/0174.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0174\nCREATE TABLE `physician` (\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `position` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `social_security_number` char(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`employee_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `department` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `head` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `department_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`head`) REFERENCES `physician` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `affiliated_with` (\n  `physician_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `department_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`physician_id`, `department_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `affiliated_with_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`physician_id`) REFERENCES `physician` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `affiliated_with_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`department_id`) REFERENCES `department` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `trained_in` (\n  `physician_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `procedure_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`physician_id`, `procedure_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `trained_in_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`physician_id`) REFERENCES `physician` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `patient` (\n  `social_security_number` char(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(15) NOT NULL,\n  `insurance_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `primary_care_physician_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`social_security_number`),\n  CONSTRAINT `patient_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`primary_care_physician_id`) REFERENCES `physician` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `nurse` (\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `position` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `registration_status` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `social_security_number` char(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`employee_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `appointments` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `patient_id` char(11) NOT NULL,\n  `nurse_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `physician_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `start_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `end_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `examination_room` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `appointments_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`patient_id`) REFERENCES `patient` (`social_security_number`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `appointments_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`nurse_id`) REFERENCES `nurse` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `appointments_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`physician_id`) REFERENCES `physician` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `medication` (\n  `code` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `brand` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`code`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `prescribes` (\n  `physician_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `patient_id` char(11) NOT NULL,\n  `medication_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `appointment_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `dose` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`physician_id`, `patient_id`, `medication_id`, `appointment_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `prescribes_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`physician_id`) REFERENCES `physician` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `prescribes_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`patient_id`) REFERENCES `patient` (`social_security_number`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `prescribes_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`medication_id`) REFERENCES `medication` (`code`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `prescribes_ibfk_4` FOREIGN KEY (`appointment_id`) REFERENCES `appointments` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `block` (\n  `floor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `block_code_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`floor_id`, `block_code_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `room` (\n  `number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `block_floor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `block_code_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `availability_status` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`number`),\n  CONSTRAINT `room_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`block_floor_id`, `block_code_id`) REFERENCES `block` (`floor_id`, `block_code_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `on_call` (\n  `nurse_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `block_floor_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`nurse_id`, `block_floor_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `on_call_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`nurse_id`) REFERENCES `nurse` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `stay` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `patient_id` char(11) NOT NULL,\n  `room_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `start_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `end_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `stay_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`patient_id`) REFERENCES `patient` (`social_security_number`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `stay_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`room_id`) REFERENCES `room` (`number`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `undergoes` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `patient_id` char(11) NOT NULL,\n  `procedure_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `stay_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `physician_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `assisting_nurse_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `undergoes_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`patient_id`) REFERENCES `patient` (`social_security_number`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `undergoes_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`procedure_id`) REFERENCES `trained_in` (`procedure_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `undergoes_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`stay_id`) REFERENCES `stay` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `undergoes_ibfk_4` FOREIGN KEY (`physician_id`) REFERENCES `physician` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `undergoes_ibfk_5` FOREIGN KEY (`assisting_nurse_id`) REFERENCES `nurse` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
